266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (This project presents an end-to-end audio source separation pipeline that transforms a mixed audio signal into isolated bass, vocal, and treble components. The process begins with signal conditioning, normalization, and STFT time-frequency analysis to prepare the audio for spectral processing. It then applies 2D spectrogram anisotropic filtering and HPSS masking to separate harmonic and percussive content while preserving important time-frequency structures. Bass and vocal stems are extracted using IIR Butterworth and linear-phase FIR filter designs, ensuring smooth low-frequency separation and phase-consistent vocal isolation. Finally, the treble subband is isolated, all components are recombined, and the output is validated in both time and frequency domains to confirm separation quality and signal integrity.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
